From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wuming <eva2show@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:00:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] desktop: account-only sign-in without Platform surfaces

DSH_DESKTOP_ACCOUNT_ONLY=1 in the platform dotenv file records dshDesktopAccountOnly in the application manifest. Such a build lets people in only by signing in to its account provider: a stored API key no longer skips the welcome window, the welcome window offers no API-key entry or skip (and their IPC handlers refuse), and windows expose no dshPlatform bridge for embedded Platform pages.

ui-settings-account gains platformAccount (default true). A deployment whose account provider is not DeepSeek Platform sets it to false to hide the balance, usage and top-up rows, the onboarding credit step (progress saved on it resumes at purpose), and the API-key alternative in the sign-in dialog.

